  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare the rigor level and reason per root CLAUDE.md section 8, then load the knowledge files above.</step>
    <step order="1">In the worktree named in the prompt, install root and affected-package dependencies, then run the affected package tests and record the result as the master baseline.</step>
    <step order="2">Apply the C-5 changes already written and verified on the ontology branch: git diff 1c56cd29b~1 1c56cd29b -- &lt;paths below&gt; | git apply. The commit is in the shared object store, so it is reachable from this worktree. Path: src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/</step>
    <step order="3">C-16: find the comment in ComposeEditor.tsx claiming useComposeCommentThreads is unreachable (line numbers may have moved), confirm the hook is live by tracing its callers, and correct the comment to state what is true.</step>
    <step order="4">Run the affected package tests and builds again and compare against the baseline. Quote both outputs.</step>
    <step order="5">Commit with a conventional-commit message ending in the line: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) &lt;noreply@anthropic.com&gt;. Push the branch and open a pull request against master, ready for review (not draft). The PR body states the item ids, says the work comes from the spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 reuse audit, and ends with: 🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)</step>
    <step order="6">Report back: the PR URL, each acceptance criterion with evidence, files changed, the baseline and after test output, and any escalation.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">Install and run package tests</tool>
    <tool name="gh">Open the pull request</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A repo-wide grep finds no composeCommentThreadsToDocxAnnotations, composeSessionCommentThreadsToDocxAnnotations or anchoredAnnotationsToDocxAnnotations outside git history.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ComposeEditor.tsx comment about useComposeCommentThreads matches the hook's real reachability, with the caller cited.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A pull request against master is open, ready for review, with the item ids in its body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the PR contains no package-lock.json changes and no file outside this task's scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The after-change test run has no failure that is absent from the master baseline run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion date="2026-10-03">PR #1117 (30f364ad3 + 01ae006c3). C-5 helpers deleted with zero production callers re-confirmed; C-16 comment corrected to cite the live caller (toolbar Add Comment toggle, ComposeEditor.tsx ~3820). Follow-up removed stale anchoredAnnotationsToDocxAnnotations mock keys from 7 ComposeWorkspace test suites; remaining grep hits are doc-comments only. Baseline 61/110 suites failed to load (unbuilt @spaarke/auth dist), after 56/110: five suites newly load because a dead import chain was cut; 0 test failures either run. The 7 edited suites do not load locally, so PR #1117 CI is where they actually execute.</completion>
  <notes>Compose is governed by ADR-049; this PR deletes dead helpers and corrects a comment, and changes no save-path behaviour.</notes>

